Package: linux-modules-nvidia
Version: {{ VER }}
Architecture: {{ ARCH }}
Maintainer: Gabriel Guillou <guillou.gabriel@gmail.com>
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Depends: daemoncores-kernel-{{ KVER }} (= {{ VER }})
Description: NVIDIA open kernel modules (GPU compute profile)
 The NVIDIA open kernel modules (nvidia.ko, nvidia-uvm, nvidia-drm,
 nvidia-modeset, nvidia-peermem) built in CI against the project kernel
 (daemoncores-kernel) — the deps/waves module pattern of the
 linux-modules entries, NOT DKMS: nothing compiles on the target. The
 deb-glob of this entry is installed by the image after the kernel layer.
 The deb carries its own runtime-knob payload (owner order 05/11 — the
 host-side dc-gpu-lxc tune is folded INTO the driver deb, no separate
 package): usr/sbin/dc-nvidia-tune (idempotent persistence mode, per-GPU
 factory-max power limit, PCIe ASPM performance policy, MPS control daemon
 for the IA profile only) and the one-shot systemd unit
 dc-nvidia-tune.service its postinst enables. The loader-policy modprobe
 dc-gpu-* confs stay the policy: the tune script consumes them, it never
 overrides the profile split.
